# KNOWN-ISSUE SF7 (expected to fail, see the .xfail file).
#
# (a8 ^ a9) ^ (a8 ^ a10) ^ (a11 ^ a12) equals a9 ^ a10 ^ a11 ^ a12, because
# a8 cancels.  The XOR-tree rebalancing of -opt delay keeps the tree leaves in
# a set, so the repeated leaf a8 is kept once instead of cancelling, and the
# netlist computes a8 ^ a9 ^ a10 ^ a11 ^ a12.  The same design is proven
# equivalent with -no_xor_tree_process and in the default (area) mode.
#
# This test asserts the correct behaviour (equivalence), so it fails today.

read_verilog ../../data/designs/xor_repeat.v
proc
design -save rtl
synth_fpga -opt delay
rename top gate
design -copy-from rtl -as gold top
miter -equiv -flatten -make_assert gold gate miter
sat -verify -prove-asserts miter
